  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Malay Beehoon",
  "text": "Malay Beehoon\n\nYield: 4\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nIngredients\n\n1 carrot (cut into matchsticks),\n\n225 g fresh prawns (peeled),\n\n120 ml chicken stock,\n\n2 tbsp dark soy sauce,\n\n175 g beansprouts,\n\n115 g mustard greens or pak choi (shredded),\n\n225 g dried rice vermicelli (soaked in lukewarm water until pliable and drained),\n\n1-2 fresh chilies (deseeded and finely sliced),\n\nFresh coriander leaves (roughly chopped).\n\nFor the rempah\n\n4 dried red chilies (soaked until soft and deseeded),\n\n4 cloves of garlic,\n\n4 shallots (chopped),\n\n25 g fresh root ginger (peeled and chopped),\n\n1 tsp ground turmeric.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Combine the ingredients for the rempah in a mortar and pestle or food processor into a paste.\n\n2. In a wok fry off the rempah in a little oil until it begins to colour and becomes fragrant.\n\n3. Toss in the carrots and cook for a few minutes.\n\n4. Add the prawns.\n\n5. Add the stock and soy sauce and cook for 1 minute.\n\n6. Add the beansprouts and mustard greens.\n\n7. Add the noodles.\n\n8. Toss well to ensure the vegetables and noodles are coated and heated through.\n\n9. Transfer to a serving plate and garnish with the sliced chilies and coriander.",
  "recipeYield": "4",
